diff --git a/packages/platform-socket.io/adapters/CODEMANIFEST b/packages/platform-socket.io/adapters/CODEMANIFEST
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fab9c09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/platform-socket.io/adapters/CODEMANIFEST
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+Imports:
+  - Types:
+      - AbstractWsAdapter
+    From: packages/websockets/adapters
+
+Annotations: |
+  Concrete AbstractWsAdapter implementation over the socket.io library: the default
+  WebSocket platform used when a gateway connects and no adapter has been set
+  explicitly via useWebSocketAdapter.
+
+---
+
+"AbstractWsAdapter::IoAdapter(appOrHttpServer: any)":
+  location: io-adapter.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Wraps a socket.io server/namespace behind the `AbstractWsAdapter` contract from
+    Imports.
+
+    `appOrHttpServer`: the owning Nest application or a raw HTTP server, forwarded
+    to `AbstractWsAdapter` from Imports
+
+  methods:
+    "create(port: number, options: any) -> server: any": |
+      Create a socket.io server bound to `port` (or to the shared HTTP server when
+      `port` is 0), or return the namespace requested inside `options` on it. Reuses
+      an externally supplied server passed inside `options` instead of creating a
+      new one when given.
+    "bindMessageHandlers(client: any, handlers: Array<any>, transform: any)": |
+      Wire each entry in `handlers` to the matching socket.io event on `client`,
+      deduplicating the internal disconnect listener across repeated calls for the
+      same client. A handler result carrying an event name is sent back to `client`;
+      otherwise it is passed to the message's acknowledgement callback, if any.
+    "bindClientDisconnect(client: any, callback: Function)": |
+      Register a one-shot socket.io disconnect listener on `client` that invokes
+      `callback`.
+    "close(server: any) -> done: Promise<void>": |
+      Notify every client connected to `server` that it is shutting down, then close
+      `server` following the base close behavior inherited from `AbstractWsAdapter`.
+
+      Algorithm:
+      1. Broadcast the shutdown notice to `server` — a socket.io broadcast reaches
+         every client currently connected to that server/namespace; if none are
+         connected this has no effect
+      2. Yield one event-loop tick so socket.io's own packet encoding/transport
+         layer actually flushes the broadcast packet before the connection is torn
+         down — closing in the same synchronous tick as the broadcast silently
+         drops the packet
+      3. If force-close-connections mode is enabled and `server` shares the
+         adapter's own HTTP server, skip closing `server` here — the shared HTTP
+         server's own close is responsible for it
+      4. Otherwise close `server` via the default `AbstractWsAdapter` close from
+         Imports
+      Requirements:
+      - A `server` with no connected clients must close exactly as before this hook
+        existed
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 16/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents the socket.io platform adapter as a concrete mutation of
+  `AbstractWsAdapter`, alongside the ws adapter, showing how each platform package
+  satisfies the shared shutdown-notice guarantee using its own library's native
+  broadcast mechanism.
